  "task": {
    "objective": "Rescue six individually conserved survivors while protecting crews and managing finite water. Every rescue has shared value and extra value to its actual rescuer and the survivor-index priority role.",
    "natural_termination": "All six survivors are resolved as rescued or lost, or all three crew health values are zero. Surviving unresolved civilians remain in the final state when all crews are disabled. Otherwise truncate at 120 live steps.",
    "interaction": "Cleared fuel blocks future orthogonal ignition, spraying changes immediate hazards, and directed water gifts change a partner resource budget. Survivor custody is exclusive and can be relayed by dropping then picking. A common finite tank, occupied cells and priorities couple rescue decisions.",
    "observation_access": "Fully observable public fire, fuel, smoke, people, supplies and events. Flat cell arrays are row-major duplicates of the corresponding native grids; fixed cell positions are determined by the public 9-by-7 grid. Visibility masks are all true. Lost survivors become inactive; their loss and final health remain in the observation."
  },
